{% from "shared/macros.md.j2" import entity_line %}
{% from "fate/_events.md.j2" import events_by_world %}
{% set distortions = [
  "ties a detail to the wrong person or place (confuses who did it)",
  "reverses the order of an event",
  "never mentions the god's price or wound, only his gift",
  "says a ban or rite was set by its own ancestors, not by the god",
  "magnifies a small event, shrinks a great loss",
  "confuses the god with another god, a hero or an animal",
  "misunderstands a word and builds the whole belief on that misunderstanding",
  "attributes something the god did to a natural phenomenon (the wind, drought, salt)"
] %}
{{ world_header }}

{% if world_events %}
WHAT REALLY HAPPENED DURING AGE {{ age }} (world by world; a people lived only what happened in its own world):
{{ events_by_world(world_events, rules.fate.voices_events_chars, rules.context.budget_trim_min_chars) | trim }}
{% else %}
WHAT REALLY HAPPENED DURING AGE {{ age }}:
{{ age_events[:rules.fate.voices_events_chars] if age_events else "(a quiet age)" }}
{% endif %}

{% if historians %}
HISTORIANS (for each, this age's account through its own people's eyes; do not open with "We …", do not repeat the opening of the previous account; the previous historian continues or their apprentice takes over{% if world_events %}; every historian tells as "we" ONLY the events of its own world, never another world's event as if it befell its own people, at most as news from afar{% endif %}):
{% for entry in historians %}
people_id {{ entry.people.id }}{% if entry.world %} (its world: {{ entry.world }}){% endif %}: {{ entity_line(entry.people) }}
{% if entry.society %}
{{ entry.society }}
{% endif %}
{% if entry.previous_opening %}
Previous historian: {{ entry.previous_historian if entry.previous_historian else "name unknown" }} (Age {{ entry.previous_age }}); the previous account opened like this: «{{ entry.previous_opening[:rules.fate.historian_opening_chars] }}…»
{% endif %}
{% if not loop.last %}

{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if beliefs %}
BELIEFS (how each people tells of this god by the name it gave him; each belief's distortion is written in the form given to it, no two beliefs use the same sentence construction):
{% for pair in beliefs %}
people_id {{ pair.people_id }} {{ pair.people_name }} → son_id {{ pair.son_id }}, in truth {{ pair.son_name }}, {{ pair.son_title }} ({{ pair.domain_1 }}/{{ pair.domain_2 }}); {% if pair.known_name %}this people calls him "{{ pair.known_name }}"{% else %}this people has not yet given him a name: give one with the sounds of the {{ pair.people_name }} people's language{% endif %}. Form of distortion: {{ distortions[(pair.people_id + pair.son_id + loop.index0) % (distortions | length)] }}.{% if pair.son_id == 0 %} He is the father of all the gods, the creator; they know him as distant, old and incomprehensible.{% elif pair.worshipped %} They worship him.{% else %} They do not worship him; they know him with hostility or fear.{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
Historians should use their own peoples' names and lexicon. Beliefs should name the god by the name the people gave him; they must not know the whole truth.
